WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.930
It's Monday, November 9, and this is the Singularity Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.490
Here's what happened in superintelligence in the last 24 hours.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.750
Robots are moving in. Amazon's working on a new home robot,

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.300
"out of the movies and into our homes."

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:28.020
In China, PrimeBOT just hit 10,000 personal robots. Double, in two weeks.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:37.490
In South Korea, almost 19 million people now use the ChatGPT app every month.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:44.450
And Claude's Korean users? Up 15-fold in a year, to about 2 million.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.680
Tencent's top AI scientist warns these models

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:51.550
will soon know enough biology to do real harm.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:57.910
And Anthropic found teams of AI agents beat solo agents at business tasks,

00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:59.720
but behave less ethically.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.200
Now, the money.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:06.670
Anthropic reportedly struck a $3.4 billion deal for gas generators.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.250
Investor Cathie Wood's shrugging off the sell-off:

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:13.060
"I always feel better when the market is worried."

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:15.610
Meanwhile,

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:21.030
staff at America's AI safety centre were reportedly asked to report to the White House.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.700
Its budget? $10 million a year,

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.450
about an eighth of Britain's. And no permanent boss.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.320
This week's AI-found quantum proof?

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:35.490
A Stanford researcher calls it "a huge result."

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.690
And Diamond Foundry grew the first single-crystal diamond 20 centimetres wide,

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:44.490
aimed at cooling AI chips.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.270
The catch? A British MP's office says half its emails are now written by AI.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:56.320
And lifelike companion robots? Buyers say they're slow and pricey.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.250
Now, the machines.

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:08.540
Six robots worked a Shanghai store for a full day: over 1,700 tasks.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:14.370
Four passed. The cleaner hit a full bin, left the store, and didn't come back.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:22.190
In Karachi, two locally built robot waiters, Robia and Jojo, are drawing crowds.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:25.020
Robots are moving in, one chore at a time.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:27.720
Spend the time they give back on each other.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.240
Zoom out, and the line only goes up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.000
Check the board: the future is running early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.030
That was 24 hours. Tomorrow will be faster.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.200
You've been watching the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.310
Stay curious. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
